#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:1
msgid "Global and User `justfile`s"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:3
msgid ""
"If you want some recipes to be available everywhere, you have a few options."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:5
msgid "Global Justfile"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:7
msgid ""
"`just --global-justfile`, or `just -g` for short, searches the following "
"paths, in-order, for a justfile:"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:10
msgid "`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/just/justfile`"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:11
msgid "`$HOME/.config/just/justfile`"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:12
msgid "`$HOME/justfile`"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:13
msgid "`$HOME/.justfile`"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:15
msgid ""
"You can put recipes that are used across many projects in a global justfile "
"to easily invoke them from any directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:18
msgid "User justfile tips"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:20
msgid ""
"You can also adopt some of the following workflows. These tips assume you’ve "
"created a `justfile` at `~/.user.justfile`, but you can put this `justfile` "
"at any convenient path on your system."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:24
msgid "Recipe Aliases"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:26
msgid ""
"If you want to call the recipes in `~/.user.justfile` by name, and don’t "
"mind creating an alias for every recipe, add the following to your shell’s "
"initialization script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:30
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"for recipe in `just --justfile ~/.user.justfile --summary`; do\n"
"  alias $recipe=\"just --justfile ~/.user.justfile --working-directory . "
"$recipe\"\n"
"done\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:36
msgid ""
"Now, if you have a recipe called `foo` in `~/.user.justfile`, you can just "
"type `foo` at the command line to run it."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:39
msgid ""
"It took me way too long to realize that you could create recipe aliases like "
"this. Notwithstanding my tardiness, I am very pleased to bring you this "
"major advance in `justfile` technology."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:43
msgid "Forwarding Alias"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:45
msgid ""
"If you’d rather not create aliases for every recipe, you can create a single "
"alias:"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:51
msgid ""
"Now, if you have a recipe called `foo` in `~/.user.justfile`, you can just "
"type `.j foo` at the command line to run it."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:54
msgid "I’m pretty sure that nobody actually uses this feature, but it’s there."
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:56
msgid "¯\\\\\\_(ツ)\\_/¯"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:58
msgid "Customization"
msgstr ""

#: src/global-and-user-justfiles.md:60
msgid ""
"You can customize the above aliases with additional options. For example, if "
"you’d prefer to have the recipes in your `justfile` run in your home "
"directory, instead of the current directory:"
msgstr ""
